 ( { In this rook ending Black should be okay after the simple } 1. Kf5 Kf7 { , but he found a more 'active' idea... } ) 
 { -KEY- } Rb5 $6 2. b4 a5 $2 3. Rc5 $1 { Giving rise to a 'two pawns stop three' scenario. } Rxc5 ( { Obviously, } 3... axb4 4. Rxb5 cxb5 5. axb4 { is terminal } ) 
 ( { while after } 3... Rb6 4. Rxa5 { , the badly placed rook on b6 spells the end for Black - Baburin. } ) 
4. bxc5 e5 5. f4 { White, on the other hand, has no problems in converting his pawn majority into a passed pawn. } exf4 6. Kf3 Kf7 7. Kxf4 Kf6 8. a4 ( { After } 8. a4 Ke6 9. g5 hxg5 10. Kxg5 { White wins in outside passed pawn fashion, so Black resigned. } ) 

 1-0

